A||||25||mrfixit58||Help me figure out how to make a full custom car for $3,000.||||10||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||12-18-2001||09:06 AM||||Ok, here's the idea. I want to make a complete custom car. I've got enough parts cars to make either a notch back, or GT car. Both will need a motor, interior and paint and custom body panels, and tires. The car will be an 87 vintage. I've got $3,000 saved for the project. I can do ALL the labor myself including fabrication for the motor,  bodywork and paint. Help me design a budget to build the car. <P>To get us started, I want to use a 4.9 or 4.5 caddy motor and I figure that conversion will eat up about $1,000. However, I do have a good running 2.8 already in the car (so feel free to use it instead of the Caddy if you need the money for other things. What next?<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Formula||12-18-2001||09:17 AM||||87 GT<P><BR>4.9 $1000<P>acrylic enamel paint with 1 clear coat $200<BR>side scoops $200<BR>quarter window scoops $200<BR>lowering springs $200<BR>tinted windows $100<BR>fog lights $40<BR>clear tailights $40 (red bulbs)<BR>fuzzy dice $20<P>wheels and tires $1000<P>there ya go!||||reg||1
