Z||000019||Posthumane||12-18-2001||08:09 PM||||Buy a good book about fiberglassing (~$50-$100), get a bunch of fiberglass resin (~$200 worth), a whole ****load of fiberglass cloth, and make yourself a completely new custom body. Spend the rest of the cash on finding and old BRM 3.0 litre H16 engine (yes, 16 cyliders), and rebuilding it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Banzai||12-18-2001||10:15 PM||||WOW!!!! $3000?? Including the $600 I paid for my car(kick ass deal)I've got almost $4000 into my car. I didn't rebuild the motor and I have barely touched on the interior or exterior. I pulled the drivetrain, checked clearances etc.,new clutch,refinished all engine and engine bay components, installed all new suspension(KYB's,full Poly,Eibachs,ball joints,tie rods)and braking components(stainless lines,calipers,pads,rotors, hardware,e-brake cables)I refinished every component under the car(except fuel  tank)and put in a new windshield.<BR>Mechanicly the car is as close to perfect as it can be. I did all the labor except the windshield. This summation includes EVERYTHING I bought to do the project so far.<P>If I had another $3000 I could finish the car.<BR>Paint-do labor myself-$350<BR>Wheels and tires-$1250<BR>4.9 coversion, Keeping manual tranny-$1400+<P>If you want a "Looker" go with new wheels and your exterior mods, If you want a "runner" go with the 4.9, a little suspension work, and some new wheels and tires. Either way it'd be a CUSTOM<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Smoooooth GT||12-18-2001||11:39 PM||||What about an extra... say $200.00 total....  Shave the trim!!!  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/0newsig_1.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                    <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||6
Z||000022||Alex4mula||12-19-2001||08:59 AM||||You can do it.<P>$800 4.9 Engine (cut that budget)<BR>$200 Paint<BR>$400 Mr mike seats<BR>$150 Interior carpet<BR>$100 Grant Steereing wheel<BR>$100 Misc interior parts & interior paint<BR>$400 IRM type rocker panels<BR>$850 17" rim & tire special pkg.<P>You can use the $400 of the rocker panels for other type of scoop/exterior mod. But... as you may already know, our budgets to modify our cars always grow twice. Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000023||mrfixit58||12-19-2001||03:27 PM||||To all you guys who have spent a TON of $$$ on your cars... I'm sorry. I can't see spending that kind of money unless I have to farm out the work. As I mentioned, I think I can do ALL the labor and still wind up with some sweet wheels. <P>Anyway, here's what I think I've come up with so far:<P>Paint and body work - $200<BR>Mr Mikes Seat covers - $400<BR>Carpet (floor and doors) - $100 (non-stock)<BR>Interior vinyl paint - $30<BR>4.9 Motor w/ Auto Tranny - $1000<BR>New Qtr windows - $325<BR>New tail lgt lens covers - $250<BR>Cut coil springs - free<BR>4-wheel alignment $60<BR>Headliner and Sunvisors (recovered) - $60 <BR>That's $2425 so far. So, unless I run across a sweet swap meet deal, I'll keep my GT wheels and plan on painting them and polishing the rims and use new tires - $350<P>Total: $2775. <P>That leaves another $225 for minor miscellaneous expenses (most likely for body prep supplies, right Roger?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). Then there is the issue of a sound system... hummm... <P>It will be tight and, hopefully, when I ready to start the project I'll have a few more $$$.<P>Thanks guys,<BR>Roy<P>||||reg||6
Z||000024||Joe Torma||12-19-2001||03:42 PM||||Hmmmm....If I had someone else build me car for me, it would cost like $60,000.<P>Doing it yourself is good.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Cozmo||12-19-2001||04:33 PM||||Roy, we think alike <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>(wonder why, we've discussed this swap for the last year or so...)<BR>Here's what I've gathered so far(except the '88 cradle adaptors and suspension stuff).<BR>'87 coupe auto nice shape $750<BR>'87 GT front and rear fascias and side aero stuff $85<BR>'88 coupe donor car (rear cradle, other msc. parts) $65<BR>cradle adaptors $100<BR>4.9 engine $750<BR>coilover rears and lowering springs $450<BR>exhaust and plumbing stuff $300<BR>I'm going to do all the work myself.<BR>I already have a decent car to start with (good wheels, tires, paint, audio etc.) and I'm at $2500 so far.<BR>Maybe $500 worth of custom scoops, wing etc.?<BR>This is going to be fun...<P>------------------<BR><B>Bob Cardone</B><BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thankssig.jpg">   <BR><B>'85 2M6 SE Targa</B>||||reg||1
